          %h1#connected_topos Connected topos
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#connected_geometric_morphism"} Connected geometric morphism
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#connected_locally_connected_morphisms"} Connected locally connected morphisms
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#connected_locally_connected_sites"} Connected locally connected sites
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#orthogonality"} Orthogonality
              %li
                %a{:href => "#examples"} Examples
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            If we view a (Grothendieck)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            as a generalized
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %em connected topos
            is a generalization of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected topological space
          %p
            More generally, a
            %em connected geometric morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon E\to F
            is a “relativized” notion of this, saying that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is “connected as a topos over
            = succeed ".\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#connected_geometric_morphism Connected geometric morphism
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon E\to F
            is
            %strong connected
            if its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
            part
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is
            %strong connected
            if the unique geometric morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                  %mo =
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to Set = Sh(*)
            is connected. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+of+sheaves"} topos of sheaves
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (or more generally a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (see C1.5.7 in the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Elephant
          %p
            Equivalently, a topos is connected if its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            geometric morphism exhibits
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+objects"} discrete objects
          %p
            Connected geometric morphisms are in particular
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective+geometric+morphism"} surjective
          %h3#connected_locally_connected_morphisms Connected locally connected morphisms
          %p
            For geometric morphisms which are also
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+geometric+morphism"} locally connected
          #PreservationOfTerminalObject.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon E\to F
              is locally connected, then it is connected if and only if the left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_!
              of the inverse image functor (which exists, since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is locally connected) preserves the terminal object.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              On the one hand, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*
              is fully faithful, then the counit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_! p^* \to \Id
              is an isomorphism, so we have
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mo !
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mo !
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_!(*) \cong p_!(p^*(*)) \cong *
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_!
              preserves the terminal object.
            %p
              On the other hand, suppose that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_!
              preserves the terminal object. Suppose also for simplicity that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo =
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F=Set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_A *
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              copies of the terminal object. But
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_!
              both preserve coproducts (since they are left adjoints) and terminal objects (since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*
              is left exact, and by assumption for
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mo !
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_!
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi A
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi A
                    %mo *
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p_!(p^*(A)) \cong p_!(p^*(\coprod_A *)) \cong \coprod_A p_!(p^*(*)) \cong \coprod_A * \cong A
            %p
              Thus, the counit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_! p^* \to \Id
              is an isomorphism, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*
              is fully faithful.
            %p
              When
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is not
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              as
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+category"} indexed categories
            %p
              (This is C3.3.3 in the
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Elephant
          %p Strengthenings of this condition include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strongly+connected+geometric+morphism"} strongly connected geometric morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mo !
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_!
                preserves all finite products, and
            %li
              %p
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totally+connected+geometric+morphism"} totally connected geometric morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mo !
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_!
                preserves all finite limits.
          %h3#connected_locally_connected_sites Connected locally connected sites
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+site"} locally connected site
              with a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+of+sheaves"} topos of sheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is (not just locally connected) but connected.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              As explained at
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+site"} locally connected site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is locally connected, the left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0\colon Sh(C) \to Set
              is simply obtained by taking
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Yoneda+lemma"} co-Yoneda lemma
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              over any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+presheaf"} representable presheaf
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
              (i.e. a terminal object in
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\lim_\to y(V) = \int^{U \in C} C(U,V) = \int^{U \in C} C(U,V) \cdot * = *
                    \\,.
            %p
              But if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has a terminal object, then that terminal object represents the terminal presheaf, which is also the terminal presheaf. Hence under these conditions,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0
              preserves the terminal object, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
              is connected.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#orthogonality Orthogonality
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Connected geometric morphisms are left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal"} orthogonal
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+geometric+morphisms"} etale geometric morphisms
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos"} Topos
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              Since the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Topos
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Topos^{op} \to Cat
              sending a topos to itself and a geometric morphism to its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image+functor"} inverse image functor
              is 2-fully-faithful (an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
              on
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-categories"} hom-categories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+morphism"} co-fully-faithful
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Topos
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Topos
            %p Therefore, for 2-categorical orthogonality it suffices to show that in any commutative (up to iso) square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp; \xrightarrow{f} &amp; B
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{p}}\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{q}}
                    \\\
                    C &amp; \xrightarrow{g} &amp; D}
            %p
              of geometric morphisms in which
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is connected and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              is etale, there exists a filler
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\colon C\to B
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mi p
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h p \cong f
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mi h
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q h \cong g
            %p
              However, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in D
              is such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \cong D/X
              (such exists by definition of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              being etale), then for any topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              equipped with a geometric morphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\colon E\to D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              are equivalent to morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} * \to k^*(X)
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is determined by a map
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi q
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *\to f^*(q^*(X)) \cong p^*(g^*(X))
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo ≅
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} * \cong p^*(p_*(*))
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*
              is fully faithful, this map comes from a map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *\to g^*(X)
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\colon C\to B
              which is the desired filler.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+geometric+morphism"} locally connected geometric morphism
              factors as a connected and locally connected geometric morphism followed by an etale one.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              Given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon E\to S
              locally connected, we can factor it as
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo !
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to S/f_!(*) \to S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
              again) and connected since it preserves the terminal object (by construction).
          %p In particular:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                (Connected, Etale) is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+system+in+a+2-category"} factorization system
                on the 2-category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi LCTopos
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LCTopos
                of toposes and locally connected geometric morphisms.
            %li
              %p
                The category of etale geometric morphisms over a base topos
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                itself, is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+2-category"} slice 2-category
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi LCTopos
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LCTopos/S
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflector"} reflector
                constructs “
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0
                of a locally connected topos.”
          %p
            These results all have generalizations to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} ∞-connected (∞,1)-toposes
          %h2#examples Examples
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gros+topos"} gros
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(CartSp)
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              – which contains the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-topos"} quasi-topos
              of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              is a locally connected site and contains a terminal object.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma : \mathcal{E} \to Set
              be a connected and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"} locally connected topos
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{E}
              a connected object,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0(X) \simeq *
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over-topos"} over-topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}/X
              is also connected and locally connected.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              For every object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}/X
              sits over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              by the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+geometric+morphism"} etale geometric morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi X
                              %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mo !
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo →
                          %mi Γ
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mi Δ
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Π
                            %mn 0
                    %mi Set
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{E}/X
                    \\stackrel{\overset{X_!}{\to}}{\stackrel{\overset{X^*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{X_*}{\to}}}
                    \\mathcal{E}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{\Pi_0}{\to}}{\stackrel{\overset{\Delta}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\Gamma}{\to}}}
                    Set
                    \\,.
            %p
              This makes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}/X
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"} locally connected topos
            %p
              Notice that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}/X
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi Id
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X \stackrel{Id}{\to} X)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is connected, then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi Id
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Pi_0 X_! (X \stackrel{Id}{\to} X)
                    \\simeq
                    \\Pi_0 X \simeq *
            %p
              and so the extra left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0 \circ X_!
              preserves the terminal object. By the
              %a{:href => "PreservationOfTerminalObject"} above proposition
              this means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}/X
              is also connected.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+geometric+morphism"} essential geometric morphism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"} locally connected topos
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} locally ∞-connected (∞,1)-topos
            %li
              %p
